<title>BRAZIL: RESEARCH ALERT- Telesp downgraded to hold.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT- Telesp downgraded to hold.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- ING Barings said in a report it downgraded Brazilian telecom company Telesp to hold from buy.</p>
<p>-- It raised Telesp's 12-month target price to $330 per 1,000 share lot from $285.</p>
<p>-- It also said it was lowering 1997 earnings per 1,000 shares estimate to $22 from $22.50 and 1998 earnings per 1,000 shares estimate to $25.7 from $28.05.</p>
<p>-- Telesp preferred shares were trading at 294 reais, down 0.34 percent.</p>
<p>(-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415)</p>
</text>
